            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Shannon Hewett"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I added more lemon and ice and it turend out great! mt daughter made it for us and we all loved it I made a diffrent lemonade and it was sooooooooooo sour, but this one not to sweet and not to sour!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "CarynG"
            },
            "reviewBody": "WAYYY too sweet! I reduced the sugar by 2/3 (1 cup sugar to every 12 small lemons) and 7 cups water. Used a food processor to slice the lemons wafer-thin and macerated the slices with the sugar., then stirred in the water. Iced individual servings rather than adding ice to the recipe.",
            "datePublished": "2018-08-19T02:46:32.740Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Rachel Maxey Goris"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Wonderful party drink. Big hit at my son’s graduation party. Looks so pretty in glass drink dispensers. I made strawberry lemonade by pureeing a cup of fresh strawberries then boiling it down about 30 minutes to reduce. I mixed the sugar into strawberry reduction to make a syrup, which combined better with the cold water. Do not make too far ahead of time as it turns bitter as the lemon slices sit.",
            "datePublished": "2020-01-25T23:58:03.390Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Charlena White De Leon"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I've made this three times (making it for forth time right now :)) and EVERYONE loves it!!! It's sweet but absolutely wonderful\n\nOkay after making this six or so times now I (like other reviewers) noticed that it gets bitter if you leave the peel/rind in for too long and have since started using my juicer to juice the lemons and then finishing with the recipe and have been able to cut back to 2C sugar and still have it be plenty sweet with the added benefit of it not getting bitter or having seeds in it. I just buy an extra lemon or two to slice to garnish the bowl for serving. :) And it makes a perfect gallon size pitcher if you'd rather do it in a pitcher than a punch bowl.",
            "datePublished": "2011-06-18T17:41:08.243Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "veggie newbie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made this for a birthday party along with another punch. The guests were tipping the decanter over trying to get out every last drop while the other punch was still half full. Such a great taste! I did 5 large lemons, half the sugar, 8 cups of water, 4 cups of ice from my ice maker.",
            "datePublished": "2014-04-12T13:46:38.870Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SUNSHINE6420"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made this for a cookout and received rave reviews from everyone! Not a lemon fan myself but I did taste it, even I liked it! I did use a potato ricer to squeeze the lemons and increased the recipe to 20 lemons and 5 cups sugar. Used a 2 quart pitcher full of ice and it got better as the evening went on! Strained the lemons out of the remaining liquid (they can turn rancid overnight)!",
            "datePublished": "2012-08-25T20:47:09.997Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "L0VEY"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is great. I tried it as is. I tried it using Splenda instead of sugar. I tried it using limes for limeade. All were good. I used a small whisk to mash up the fruit. I thought it was a good idea to wash the fruit before slicing it, since the peel remains in the mixture.",
            "datePublished": "2009-06-06T12:39:41.827Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "lizzyd"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I've made this recipe a couple of times now and it's always turned out very well. Most recently, instead of using 12 lemons I used 6 lemons and 6 limes for lemon-limeade, and it is fabulous! I also used 2 cups of sugar instead of 3 and it is still sweet enough.",
            "datePublished": "2013-03-17T17:12:30.443Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Michael Seaman"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Add mashed organic strawberries. Its amazing. I only use 3 large lemons and one cup of sugar for a half gallon.",
            "datePublished": "2013-07-06T18:57:46.530Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Brittney Ann"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great recipe! Instead of mashing the lemons with the sugar I juiced my lemons with a juicer (saved 2 for slicing) mixed the sugar, added water and iced cubes and then added lemon slices to the lemonade and chilled for a half hour. Superb thanks for sharing! \n\nIf anyone tries this make sure to remove the sliced lemons from the lemonade at the end of the day. The lemons make the lemonade bitter if in there for too long.",
            "datePublished": "2013-04-07T13:14:52.110Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "jan p"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used 6 lemons, 1 cup of honey granules, placed in a 2 qt jar and filled with water. Love it!",
            "datePublished": "2012-08-06T14:53:12.497Z"
